{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 52, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ושרף את הבגד", :translit "v'saraf et ha-beged", :gloss "and he shall burn the garment"} {:he "הפסוק מתחיל ומסיים בשרפה", :translit "ha-pasuk matchil u'msayem bi-sreifah", :gloss "the verse begins and ends with burning"} {:he "כל האסורים בהנאה טעונין שרפה", :translit "kol ha-asurim be-hana'ah ta'unin sreifah", :gloss "all forbidden for benefit require burning"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Inclusive reading: verse opens (v'saraf) and closes (ba-esh tisaref, Lev 13:55) with the same root שרף"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'all things forbidden for benefit require burning' is a Tannaitic principle: when an item becomes forbidden through a prohibitive decree (e.g., an affected garment, leaven on Passover, or idolatrous objects), it must be destroyed by fire. Ba'al HaTurim derives this specifically for the garment-affliction of Leviticus 13:52 from the literary envelope of the root שרף at both ends of the passage.", :sources ["Leviticus 13:52" "Leviticus 13:55" "Pesachim 21b" "Shabbat 25b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Inclusive reading: verse opens (v'saraf) and closes (ba-esh tisaref, Lev 13:55) with the same root שרף", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:23:20.181942555Z", :model "glm-5.2"}